[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a new project in an essentially empty repo — no React, no build tooling, just two stub JS files. That makes it
  [1marchitectural[0m, so I'll work through clarifying questions → approaches → a design you approve → a spec, before any
  code gets written.

  Let me start with the question that shapes everything else.

  [1mThe fork:[0m whether the todo list keeps data between page loads, and where. This is the one choice that's expensive to
  change later, because it determines whether there's a backend at all.

  - [1mIn-memory only[0m — simplest possible; state resets on refresh. Fine for a demo or a UI exercise. Rules out
    multi-device use.
  - [1mlocalStorage[0m — persists per-browser, still zero backend. Cheap to add later, cheap to remove. Rules out sharing
    between devices/users.
  - [1mReal backend + database[0m — persists everywhere, supports accounts later. Costs an API, a server, deployment, and
    roughly 3-4× the work. Adding this later means rewriting how the UI loads and mutates data.

  My recommendation is [1mlocalStorage[0m: it makes the app feel real (your todos survive a refresh) without dragging in a
  server, and it's a clean seam to swap for an API later if you ever want one.
